Feature: tour viewer
  As a reviewer
  I want to step through a tour's slides while Neovim follows along
  So that I can read a narrated walkthrough of a code change

  @ft:13
  Scenario: Launching shows the first slide
    Given a valid .tour file with three slides
    When I launch `tour` on it
    Then it displays the first slide's narration
    And it shows "1 of 3" as the position

  @ft:14
  Scenario: Advancing to the next slide
    Given the viewer is showing slide 1 of 3
    When I press the next-slide key
    Then it displays slide 2's narration
    And it shows "2 of 3" as the position

  @ft:15
  Scenario: Going back to the previous slide
    Given the viewer is showing slide 2 of 3
    When I press the previous-slide key
    Then it displays slide 1's narration
    And it shows "1 of 3" as the position

  @ft:16
  Scenario: Stepping past the last slide is a no-op
    Given the viewer is showing the last slide
    When I press the next-slide key
    Then it still shows the last slide

  @ft:17
  Scenario: Stepping before the first slide is a no-op
    Given the viewer is showing the first slide
    When I press the previous-slide key
    Then it still shows the first slide

  @ft:18
  Scenario: Jumping directly to a slide number
    Given the viewer is showing slide 1 of 9
    When I enter the jump-to-slide command for slide 5
    Then it displays slide 5's narration directly, without stepping through 2, 3, and 4

  @ft:19
  Scenario: Jumping to the first slide
    Given the viewer is showing the last slide of a multi-slide tour
    When I press the jump-to-first-slide key
    Then it displays the first slide's narration

  @ft:20
  Scenario: Jumping to the last slide
    Given the viewer is showing the first slide of a multi-slide tour
    When I press the jump-to-last-slide key
    Then it displays the last slide's narration

  @ft:21
  Scenario: Scrolling the body does not change the current slide
    Given the viewer is showing slide 2 of 3 with narration too long to fit on screen
    When I press the scroll-down key
    Then it still shows "2 of 3" as the position

  @ft:22
  Scenario: Scroll position resets when the slide changes
    Given the viewer is showing slide 1 scrolled partway down its narration
    When I advance to slide 2
    Then slide 2's narration is shown from the top

  @ft:23
  Scenario: Advancing a slide jumps Neovim to its location
    Given the viewer is connected to a running Neovim
    When I advance to a slide pointing at "lib/app.rb:42"
    Then Neovim's cursor moves to lib/app.rb line 42

  @ft:24
  Scenario: No Neovim session found still shows the narration
    Given no Neovim session can be located
    When I launch `tour` on a valid tour file
    Then it displays the first slide's narration
    And it clearly indicates that no Neovim session was found

  @ft:25
  Scenario: A structural error prevents the tour from opening
    Given a .tour file with a structural error
    When I launch `tour` on it
    Then it reports every structural error found
    And it does not open the viewer

  @ft:26
  Scenario: A location error does not prevent the tour from opening
    Given a .tour file where one slide's location does not resolve
    When I launch `tour` on it
    Then the viewer opens normally
    And landing on the affected slide shows the location error instead of its file:line
